    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of the square, we need to first determine the length of its side. According to the problem, the length of the side of the square can be expressed in two different ways: \\(4x - 15\\) meters and \\(20 - 3x\\) meters. Since both expressions represent the same length, we can set them equal to each other and solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n4x - 15 = 20 - 3x\n\\]\n\nNext, we will solve this equation step-by-step to find the value of \\(x\\).\n\n1. Add \\(3x\\) to both sides to combine like terms:\n\\[\n4x + 3x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\n2. Simplify:\n\\[\n7x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\n3. Add 15 to both sides to isolate \\(7x\\):\n\\[\n7x = 20 + 15\n\\]\n\n4. Simplify:\n\\[\n7x = 35\n\\]\n\n5. Divide both sides by 7 to solve for \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx = \\frac{35}{7}\n\\]\n\n6. Simplify:\n\\[\nx = 5\n\\]\n\nNow that we have the value of \\(x\\), we can substitute it back into either expression for the side length to find the actual length of the side of the square. Let's use \\(4x - 15\\):\n\n\\[\n4(5) - 15 = 20 - 15 = 5 \\text{ meters}\n\\]\n\nThe side length of the square is 5 meters. The area of a square is given by the square of its side length. Therefore, the area \\(A\\) is:\n\n\\[\nA = 5^2 = 25 \\text{ square meters}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the square is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{25}\n\\]",
