      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the area of the square, we need to determine the length of its side. Given that the edge of the square can be expressed as \\(4x-15\\) meters or as \\(20-3x\\) meters, we can set these two expressions equal to each other and solve for \\(x\\).\n\nFirst, we set the expressions equal to each other:\n\\[\n4x - 15 = 20 - 3x\n\\]\n\nNext, we solve for \\(x\\). To do this, we first add \\(3x\\) to both sides of the equation:\n\\[\n4x + 3x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\\[\n7x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\nThen, we add 15 to both sides:\n\\[\n7x = 35\n\\]\n\nFinally, we divide both sides by 7:\n\\[\nx = 5\n\\]\n\nNow that we have the value of \\(x\\), we can substitute it back into either expression for the side length of the square. We use \\(4x - 15\\):\n\\[\n4(5) - 15 = 20 - 15 = 5\n\\]\n\nSo, the side length of the square is 5 meters. The area of a square is the side length squared:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = 5^2 = 25 \\text{ square meters}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{25}\\) square meters.",
