      "text": "To find the area of the square, we first need to determine the length of one of its sides. Given that the side length can be expressed in two different ways, we can set these expressions equal to each other and solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n4x - 15 = 20 - 3x\n\\]\n\nLet's solve this equation step by step:\n\n1. Add \\(3x\\) to both sides to combine like terms:\n\\[\n4x + 3x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\\[\n7x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\n2. Add 15 to both sides to isolate the term with \\(x\\):\n\\[\n7x - 15 + 15 = 20 + 15\n\\]\n\\[\n7x = 35\n\\]\n\n3. Divide both sides by 7 to solve for \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx = \\frac{35}{7}\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 5\n\\]\n\nNow that we have the value of \\(x\\), we can substitute it back into one of the original expressions for the side length to find the actual length of the side of the square. Using \\(4x - 15\\):\n\n\\[\n4(5) - 15 = 20 - 15 = 5\n\\]\n\nSo, the side length of the square is 5 meters.\n\nNext, we calculate the area of the square by squaring the side length:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = 5^2 = 25 \\text{ square meters}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{25}\\) square meters.",
